# unknownop.poke -- an opcode this broker does not implement is RECOVERABLE.
#
# Every frame is length prefixed, so the broker consumes the payload and the
# stream stays in step. That is the forward compatibility path for a program
# written against a later minor version, and making it fatal would destroy
# it. This program asks for op 0x7e, is told NOSUCHOP, and carries on to
# exit cleanly -- which is the whole point.
#   hello  op 01, len 10, magic "BSTM", want major 1, want minor 0, flags 0
EMIT 01 0a 00 42 53 54 4d 01 00 00 00 00 00
READ 107
#   op 7e does not exist; the reply is a bare status with no payload
EMIT 7e 00 00
READ 3
#   exit  op 02, len 1, code 0 -- the conversation survived the unknown op
EMIT 02 01 00 00
READ 3
